1
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:46,463
There are more than 200,000 men…

2
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:48,840
And the Toyotomi?

3
00:00:50,175 --> 00:00:51,259
73,000.

4
00:00:57,932 --> 00:00:58,933
Are you all right?

5
00:00:59,017 --> 00:00:59,851
Yeah.

6
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:02,062
Make sure you take care of yourself.

7
00:01:03,229 --> 00:01:05,732
I really want you to open
that restaurant someday, Seikai.

8
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:09,736
Well, I want you to make your dream
come true too, brother.

9
00:01:10,862 --> 00:01:14,157
SECRET TALKS - TAISEIJI TEMPLE

10
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:27,295
Hey… you lot.

11
00:01:29,631 --> 00:01:30,965
What have you done to them?

12
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:32,634
Hey!

13
00:01:33,426 --> 00:01:34,260
Release me!

14
00:01:34,844 --> 00:01:36,554
Get these damn things off!

15
00:01:37,639 --> 00:01:39,015
Don't just stand there!

16
00:01:40,725 --> 00:01:41,559
You bastard!

17
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:46,564
Hattori Hanzo…

18
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:49,192
You'll pay for what you did
to the old man.

19
00:01:50,652 --> 00:01:51,945
I'll kill you!

20
00:01:52,028 --> 00:01:53,655
You know this one, Hanzo?

21
00:01:53,738 --> 00:01:55,865
He was the ninja under Hakuunsai.

22
00:01:56,908 --> 00:01:59,202
So this is the one you failed to kill.

23
00:02:02,205 --> 00:02:03,123
Magnificent.

24
00:02:04,541 --> 00:02:06,000
So you're Ieyasu.

25
00:02:07,293 --> 00:02:09,671
A ninja who can leap
across a river 30 ken wide.

26
00:02:10,255 --> 00:02:12,882
With the right training,
he could leap even farther.

27
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:15,009
All the better,

28
00:02:15,927 --> 00:02:17,887
since our beast has yet to awaken.

29
00:02:18,847 --> 00:02:20,473
-What?
-Ninja.

30
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:22,684
Come serve me.

31
00:02:23,810 --> 00:02:26,437
I don't take orders from anyone!

32
00:02:27,063 --> 00:02:28,773
I'll give you whatever your heart desires.

33
00:02:29,691 --> 00:02:30,775
What do you want?

34
00:02:31,734 --> 00:02:32,652
Money?

35
00:02:33,862 --> 00:02:34,821
Women?

36
00:02:35,822 --> 00:02:38,241
The Ogosho himself is offering you
a place in his service.

37
00:02:39,409 --> 00:02:40,285
Hey.

38
00:02:40,994 --> 00:02:43,079
There could be no greater honor.

39
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:46,916
Who the hell are you?

40
00:02:47,709 --> 00:02:49,586
Stay out of this, small fry!

41
00:02:58,720 --> 00:02:59,804
That reminds me.

42
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:02,223
I heard something about you.

43
00:03:02,682 --> 00:03:04,642
You've got a taste
for Western food, haven't you?

44
00:03:05,894 --> 00:03:08,396
I've always wanted to try some.

45
00:03:09,272 --> 00:03:11,649
What was it called again?

46
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:15,945
Tempura?

47
00:03:19,032 --> 00:03:21,576
All that searching,
and still no sign of him.

48
00:03:23,453 --> 00:03:25,788
Where on earth is Sasuke?

49
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:29,751
Maybe that monkey
ran back to the mountains.

50
00:03:31,085 --> 00:03:33,755
I can't imagine him giving up on revenge.

51
00:03:33,838 --> 00:03:36,299
Who cares? Let him do as he pleases.

52
00:03:36,382 --> 00:03:38,635
Of all times for Sasuke to disappear…

53
00:03:41,846 --> 00:03:42,805
Hey…

54
00:03:44,891 --> 00:03:46,351
Have you seen Isa or Seikai?

55
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:50,772
Mind if I ask you something?

56
00:03:51,648 --> 00:03:55,401
Can a ninja change masters?

57
00:03:56,819 --> 00:03:59,155
Well… it's not unheard of.

58
00:03:59,948 --> 00:04:01,532
-I see.
-Don't write it down.

59
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:06,204
My lord, about the name of our outpost…

60
00:04:06,287 --> 00:04:07,747
What? Now?

61
00:04:08,456 --> 00:04:09,916
You entrusted me with a great task.

62
00:04:09,999 --> 00:04:13,378
I, Mochizuki,
have spent the entire night pondering it.

63
00:04:14,921 --> 00:04:16,339
Have you come up with a good name?

64
00:04:19,175 --> 00:04:21,678
How does "Sanadamaru" sound?

65
00:04:21,761 --> 00:04:22,679
That's too obvious!

66
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:24,681
I rather like it.

67
00:04:25,682 --> 00:04:29,018
What better name to show the world
the might of the Sanada?

68
00:04:29,602 --> 00:04:30,436
Yes, my lord.

69
00:04:34,023 --> 00:04:35,900
-It's one of the Toyotomi retainers.
-Wait.

70
00:04:36,901 --> 00:04:37,944
There's no need to hide.

71
00:04:47,078 --> 00:04:48,705
Perhaps you weren't aware.

72
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:52,959
Ninja are forbidden
within the castle walls.

73
00:04:53,501 --> 00:04:56,087
We have Lord Hideyori's permission.

74
00:04:58,256 --> 00:05:01,426
So you've even managed
to win Lord Hideyori over.

75
00:05:02,343 --> 00:05:05,179
You truly are a master of intrigue.

76
00:05:06,014 --> 00:05:07,515
I heard the news.

77
00:05:09,892 --> 00:05:12,395
Some of your retainers have deserted you.

78
00:05:13,563 --> 00:05:15,273
Come to think of it…

79
00:05:16,149 --> 00:05:19,110
Where's that cocky monkey of yours?

80
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:21,487
That's the trouble with ninja.

81
00:05:22,739 --> 00:05:25,366
They know the castle's inner workings.

82
00:05:25,908 --> 00:05:28,077
We cannot risk them
defecting to the enemy.

83
00:05:28,661 --> 00:05:31,331
I trust you'll see
that they're dealt with.

84
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:34,417
They would never betray us.

85
00:05:34,500 --> 00:05:38,046
I doubt ninja who serve for money
know much of loyalty.

86
00:05:38,796 --> 00:05:40,006
You need not worry.

87
00:05:41,299 --> 00:05:44,552
We shall claim victory at the outpost.

88
00:05:44,635 --> 00:05:45,928
You have my word.

89
00:05:48,431 --> 00:05:50,725
ONO HARUNAGA

90
00:05:50,808 --> 00:05:52,310
About that…

91
00:05:53,352 --> 00:05:55,938
I've been placed in command
of all our forces.

92
00:05:56,939 --> 00:05:58,149
The outpost included.

93
00:06:00,318 --> 00:06:01,944
After the recent incident,

94
00:06:02,487 --> 00:06:06,699
many have questioned whether Sanada
can be trusted, given his use of ninja.

95
00:06:06,783 --> 00:06:08,701
I'm afraid I had little choice.

96
00:06:09,994 --> 00:06:11,370
From now on,

97
00:06:12,121 --> 00:06:14,499
you'll be taking your orders from me.

98
00:06:17,877 --> 00:06:19,378
SANADAMARU

99
00:06:21,672 --> 00:06:23,049
"Sanadamaru."

100
00:06:28,054 --> 00:06:30,723
You named the fortress after yourself.

101
00:06:30,807 --> 00:06:31,933
ODA URAKUSAI

102
00:06:32,016 --> 00:06:33,810
I suppose I can see why.

103
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:35,895
But…

104
00:06:36,437 --> 00:06:39,649
you'd best live up to that name.

105
00:06:46,697 --> 00:06:49,617
I understand your desire
for glory in battle,

106
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:53,162
but this is the Toyotomi's war.

107
00:06:54,330 --> 00:06:55,873
Do not…

108
00:06:56,958 --> 00:06:58,126
forget your place.

109
00:07:08,803 --> 00:07:10,012
Fear not.

110
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:13,266
Once we have the outpost,
we'll be ready to fight at any moment.

111
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:22,733
Aren't you going to consult your dice
like you always do?

112
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:27,321
They haven't been much help lately.

113
00:07:35,121 --> 00:07:36,831
If Sasuke were here…

114
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:40,376
he'd have given him a piece of his mind.

115
00:07:55,016 --> 00:07:56,100
Damn, this is good!

116
00:07:58,811 --> 00:08:02,565
There's something
I wish to discuss with the Ogosho.

117
00:08:02,648 --> 00:08:03,483
Well?

118
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:06,611
Have you decided to serve me?

119
00:08:07,737 --> 00:08:09,447
I'm still pretty torn.

120
00:08:11,574 --> 00:08:15,620
By the way, why are you
so bent on wiping out the Toyotomi?

121
00:08:17,205 --> 00:08:19,081
-This is good!
-To bring peace to the land.

122
00:08:20,082 --> 00:08:21,250
And to do that,

123
00:08:21,334 --> 00:08:24,128
all who oppose me must be eliminated.

124
00:08:25,213 --> 00:08:28,799
Only absolute power can keep the peace.

125
00:08:30,718 --> 00:08:32,637
Well, well. Lord Hidetada.

126
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:36,516
So this is Sanada's ninja.

127
00:08:39,310 --> 00:08:41,812
Father, allow me to kill him.

128
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:47,568
You surely haven't forgotten
what he did to me at Ueda?

129
00:08:47,652 --> 00:08:51,739
So you're the idiot son
who lost to a mere thousand Sanada troops.

130
00:08:51,822 --> 00:08:53,282
Not a thousand! Two thousand!

131
00:08:54,575 --> 00:08:55,743
How dare you…

132
00:08:56,911 --> 00:08:57,745
Enough!

133
00:08:58,704 --> 00:09:01,123
The man you should be killing
is Sanada Yukimura.

134
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:04,335
You talk a big game,

135
00:09:05,211 --> 00:09:07,672
but you're just bitter
about losing to Sanada, aren't you?

136
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:10,132
Ogosho.

137
00:09:10,216 --> 00:09:15,471
I agree with Lord Hidetada.
This ninja should be put to death.

138
00:09:16,305 --> 00:09:20,351
He may well become a threat to us one day.

139
00:09:20,434 --> 00:09:22,687
He is my ninja.

140
00:09:30,194 --> 00:09:32,822
Know your place, Hanzo.

141
00:09:33,656 --> 00:09:34,782
Wait!

142
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:36,576
Another serving!

143
00:09:38,619 --> 00:09:40,580
I understand your concerns.

144
00:09:41,414 --> 00:09:44,375
But remember,
you're dealing with the Ogosho himself.

145
00:09:45,126 --> 00:09:46,002
Tread carefully.

146
00:09:46,877 --> 00:09:47,712
Yes, sir.

147
00:09:49,088 --> 00:09:50,464
What of Sanada?

148
00:09:50,548 --> 00:09:52,842
He appears to be preparing for battle.

149
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:54,260
Keep a close watch on him.

150
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:55,720
Yes, sir.

151
00:09:56,846 --> 00:09:58,764
Once this creature awakens,

152
00:09:59,599 --> 00:10:01,601
the tide of battle will turn.

153
00:10:02,393 --> 00:10:06,564
And then, we'll have no further need
for Sanada's ninja.

154
00:10:08,149 --> 00:10:10,109
How much longer do you intend to sleep?

155
00:10:42,141 --> 00:10:43,267
Hey, Saizo.

156
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:47,855
What did Hattori Hanzo
say to you back then?

157
00:10:52,943 --> 00:10:55,029
Ninja are despised

158
00:10:55,738 --> 00:10:58,532
and used as pawns by the Toyotomi,
only to die in the end.

159
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:00,910
Join the Tokugawa.

160
00:11:01,952 --> 00:11:04,455
He said the Toyotomi would use us
as pawns and leave us to die.

161
00:11:05,539 --> 00:11:06,874
That it was my fate.

162
00:11:10,461 --> 00:11:11,796
He may be right.

163
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:16,675
But…

164
00:11:18,094 --> 00:11:20,179
I have to fight all the same.

165
00:11:23,057 --> 00:11:24,058
Saizo.

166
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:28,354
What do you fight for?

167
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:33,567
I…

168
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:50,584
What's this?

169
00:11:51,585 --> 00:11:54,505
Goto will defend the main bailey.

170
00:11:54,588 --> 00:11:57,133
Kimura and Chosokabe will hold Hatchome.

171
00:11:58,217 --> 00:12:00,136
Akashi, the Kizugawa approach.

172
00:12:00,719 --> 00:12:02,263
Hold your positions at all costs.

173
00:12:03,139 --> 00:12:05,307
No acting on your own!

174
00:12:06,183 --> 00:12:07,143
Understood?

175
00:12:07,226 --> 00:12:08,394
Yes, sir.

176
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:15,818
Why must we take orders
from a man who's never seen battle?

177
00:12:15,901 --> 00:12:16,986
GOTO MATABEI

178
00:12:17,069 --> 00:12:18,737
And the ronin?

179
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:21,240
How is their morale?

180
00:12:23,701 --> 00:12:25,578
They may be a ragtag bunch,

181
00:12:26,245 --> 00:12:28,664
but I have them under control.

182
00:12:28,747 --> 00:12:30,040
You need not worry.

183
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:32,918
And Sanada?

184
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:38,174
He's building the outpost as ordered.

185
00:12:38,841 --> 00:12:40,468
Everything is proceeding smoothly.

186
00:12:45,431 --> 00:12:46,640
Just a little more!

187
00:12:51,103 --> 00:12:51,937
Good work.

188
00:12:52,021 --> 00:12:55,024
Ono seems to be struggling
to keep the ronin in line.

189
00:12:55,691 --> 00:12:56,692
Hardly surprising.

190
00:12:57,485 --> 00:12:59,945
He may be skilled in castle politics,

191
00:13:00,029 --> 00:13:02,239
but he has never fought a battle.

192
00:13:02,990 --> 00:13:06,243
How could he possibly command the ronin?

193
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:09,788
At this rate,
we'll lose a war we could've won.

194
00:13:10,956 --> 00:13:13,334
We must focus on what we can do.

195
00:13:15,002 --> 00:13:16,921
Good work, everyone.

196
00:13:17,004 --> 00:13:19,757
Lord Yukimura! It's been so long!

197
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:20,925
Okuni.

198
00:13:21,008 --> 00:13:23,010
So you're all together.

199
00:13:23,093 --> 00:13:24,678
I'm glad you're safe.

200
00:13:24,762 --> 00:13:27,515
I heard your village was burned down.
What happened to the others?

201
00:13:28,307 --> 00:13:29,391
I don't know.

202
00:13:29,975 --> 00:13:31,560
I just ran for my life…

203
00:13:32,394 --> 00:13:34,563
You escaped the village alone?

204
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:40,736
I was so scared… I'm sorry.

205
00:13:41,403 --> 00:13:44,323
No, it's all right. Forgive me.

206
00:13:46,033 --> 00:13:47,326
So that's how you ended up here?

207
00:13:47,868 --> 00:13:51,664
I was fortunate enough to be taken in.
I work here at the castle now.

208
00:13:52,706 --> 00:13:53,874
If you'll excuse me.

209
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:58,379
-Please, everyone, help yourselves.
-Lord Yukimura.

210
00:14:17,690 --> 00:14:18,774
Look at this.

211
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:24,738
This is Sasuke's Muramasa sword…

212
00:14:25,948 --> 00:14:29,660
A townsman claimed
he'd seen someone resembling Sasuke.

213
00:14:29,743 --> 00:14:31,996
We searched the area,
and found this nearby.

214
00:14:32,913 --> 00:14:35,207
Something may have happened to Sasuke.

215
00:14:36,542 --> 00:14:39,044
The Tokugawa may have captured him.

216
00:14:40,129 --> 00:14:41,171
What makes you think that?

217
00:14:43,299 --> 00:14:44,258
Saizo…

218
00:14:45,217 --> 00:14:46,552
encountered Hanzo.

219
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:49,763
But Hanzo made no attempt to kill him.

220
00:14:51,348 --> 00:14:54,143
It's possible.
He may have wanted to use him.

221
00:14:56,228 --> 00:14:58,355
Judging by what happened to Lady Okurakyo…

222
00:15:01,483 --> 00:15:04,904
the Tokugawa may have
a ninja who can control minds.

223
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:08,699
You think they're trying
to turn Sasuke against us?

224
00:15:12,995 --> 00:15:14,121
Saizo, a word.

225
00:15:15,122 --> 00:15:15,998
Yes, my lord.

226
00:15:20,210 --> 00:15:24,006
Once the battle begins,
the enemy's defenses should weaken.

227
00:15:25,674 --> 00:15:28,636
I want you to use that chance
to rescue Sasuke.

228
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:33,849
It will be a dangerous mission.

229
00:15:34,558 --> 00:15:35,684
Can I count on you?

230
00:15:50,491 --> 00:15:52,618
I am Urano Motokuni.

231
00:15:54,286 --> 00:15:57,831
His family has been related to ours
since my grandfather's time.

232
00:15:57,915 --> 00:16:00,793
He's our most trusted samurai.

233
00:16:01,502 --> 00:16:04,505
I can't leave the outpost
in Sanada's hands alone,

234
00:16:05,214 --> 00:16:08,008
so he'll be stationed there as well.

235
00:16:08,092 --> 00:16:09,927
That is most reassuring.

236
00:16:10,761 --> 00:16:11,971
I'm counting on you.

237
00:16:12,054 --> 00:16:12,888
Yes, my lady.

238
00:16:12,972 --> 00:16:15,391
I've brought my finest men.

239
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:20,229
We'll defend the outpost with our lives.

240
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:43,502
So even tempura
wasn't enough to win him over.

241
00:16:44,753 --> 00:16:48,924
I even threw in an extra-large shrimp.
You rarely come across one of those.

242
00:16:52,052 --> 00:16:53,887
That should make him cooperate.

243
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:56,015
Now…

244
00:16:57,558 --> 00:16:59,893
write, Sasuke.

245
00:17:01,854 --> 00:17:04,064
Write down everything you've seen.

246
00:17:07,234 --> 00:17:08,152
Yes.

247
00:17:37,931 --> 00:17:38,974
Well done.

248
00:17:41,393 --> 00:17:42,227
Here.

249
00:17:52,362 --> 00:17:54,239
What did Lord Yukimura ask you to do?

250
00:17:55,324 --> 00:17:56,617
Is it about Sasuke?

251
00:18:02,289 --> 00:18:03,123
Yuri.

252
00:18:04,374 --> 00:18:05,709
Remember what we talked about?

253
00:18:08,045 --> 00:18:10,631
What we'd do when this war's over?

254
00:18:17,346 --> 00:18:20,641
If I make it back alive,
there's something I want to tell you.

255
00:18:51,421 --> 00:18:53,841
Are you ready for battle?

256
00:18:54,508 --> 00:18:55,342
Yes, sir!

257
00:18:55,425 --> 00:18:59,012
We'll defend this outpost at all costs!

258
00:18:59,096 --> 00:19:00,889
Ei! Ei! Oh!

259
00:19:00,973 --> 00:19:03,350
Ei! Ei! Oh!

260
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:04,977
Ei! Ei! Oh!

261
00:19:05,602 --> 00:19:07,604
Ei! Ei! Oh!

262
00:19:10,315 --> 00:19:12,192
I am Urano Motokuni.

263
00:19:13,694 --> 00:19:15,737
It is an honor to fight

264
00:19:15,821 --> 00:19:19,575
alongside the man
who twice defeated Lord Ieyasu.

265
00:19:20,534 --> 00:19:23,078
I'm grateful for your support.

266
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:25,664
Urano comes from a distinguished family.

267
00:19:26,373 --> 00:19:29,501
Unlike the ninja,
he's a man you can trust.

268
00:19:30,085 --> 00:19:34,047
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I have preparations to make.

269
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:43,557
Will the Ogosho
truly take me into his service?

270
00:19:47,853 --> 00:19:49,771
You have the Ogosho's word.

271
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:52,065
There's no doubt about it.

272
00:19:52,983 --> 00:19:54,067
See that you don't fail.

273
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:55,944
I know what I'm doing.

274
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:04,244
On the day of battle,

275
00:20:05,245 --> 00:20:08,207
my men will stage a revolt
inside the outpost…

276
00:20:08,790 --> 00:20:10,334
Then send up a smoke signal.

277
00:20:10,417 --> 00:20:11,376
I see.

278
00:20:11,793 --> 00:20:13,712
Once we see that signal, we'll attack.

279
00:20:13,795 --> 00:20:16,173
We'll have them trapped
from within and without.

280
00:20:17,132 --> 00:20:19,218
The outpost will fall in no time.

281
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:23,597
Their greatest hope for victory
will be the first to fall.

282
00:20:24,348 --> 00:20:25,849
How pitiful.

283
00:20:26,808 --> 00:20:30,312
I can barely contain my excitement
at the thought of killing Sanada.

284
00:20:32,147 --> 00:20:33,273
Father.

285
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:35,734
Please allow me to lead the vanguard!

286
00:20:35,817 --> 00:20:37,361
SHUN THIS WORLD, SEEK THE PURE LAND

287
00:20:37,444 --> 00:20:38,445
Hidetada.

288
00:20:39,947 --> 00:20:41,615
How do we count shrimp?

289
00:20:42,699 --> 00:20:43,659
By their tails.

290
00:20:43,742 --> 00:20:44,576
Indeed.

291
00:20:45,994 --> 00:20:46,828
And birds?

292
00:20:47,746 --> 00:20:48,664
By their feathers.

293
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:50,540
We count living creatures

294
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:53,252
by what they leave behind in death.

295
00:20:54,795 --> 00:20:56,463
Then what of men?

296
00:20:57,714 --> 00:20:58,590
By their names.

297
00:21:00,175 --> 00:21:02,344
A man's name is what lives on.

298
00:21:03,804 --> 00:21:05,806
Redeem yourself in this battle.

299
00:21:06,807 --> 00:21:08,725
Make a name for yourself, Hidetada.

300
00:21:09,434 --> 00:21:10,435
Yes, Father!

301
00:21:14,731 --> 00:21:16,316
Make way, everyone!

302
00:21:17,943 --> 00:21:20,237
Her Ladyship has come
to encourage the troops.

303
00:21:23,115 --> 00:21:23,991
All of you,

304
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:26,493
fight to your last breath.

305
00:21:28,036 --> 00:21:30,330
You must defend the Toyotomi!

306
00:21:30,414 --> 00:21:31,540
Yes, my lady.

307
00:21:31,623 --> 00:21:34,167
What does she think our lives are worth?

308
00:21:35,711 --> 00:21:36,920
I'm counting on you.

309
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:38,213
Yes, my lady…

310
00:21:46,096 --> 00:21:49,308
That should raise the ronin's spirits.

311
00:21:49,391 --> 00:21:50,350
Indeed.

312
00:21:50,434 --> 00:21:52,436
We are most grateful for your kindness.

313
00:21:52,519 --> 00:21:55,105
Victory is all but assured.

314
00:22:06,658 --> 00:22:07,993
The time has finally come.

315
00:22:08,994 --> 00:22:10,495
Fourteen years in Kudoyama…

316
00:22:11,455 --> 00:22:12,998
All for this day.

317
00:22:23,050 --> 00:22:25,343
I've kept you all waiting long enough.

318
00:22:39,858 --> 00:22:40,942
Let's do this.

319
00:22:55,332 --> 00:22:57,084
A smoke signal from the outpost!

320
00:23:01,171 --> 00:23:03,048
Good.

321
00:23:05,509 --> 00:23:06,384
What's happening?

322
00:23:12,766 --> 00:23:14,434
Urgent news!

323
00:23:15,685 --> 00:23:17,479
-We've got trouble!
-What is it?

324
00:23:17,562 --> 00:23:19,397
There's a revolt inside the outpost!

325
00:23:20,357 --> 00:23:21,316
Then…

326
00:23:21,900 --> 00:23:23,110
that smoke signal is…

327
00:23:24,027 --> 00:23:27,364
It must be… a signal to the Tokugawa.

328
00:23:28,448 --> 00:23:29,866
What does this mean?

329
00:23:29,950 --> 00:23:32,410
What is going on? Harunaga!

330
00:23:32,994 --> 00:23:34,579
Yes, my lady! Excuse me!

331
00:23:43,463 --> 00:23:45,507
Well then, shall we begin?

332
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:50,011
Our first battle since Sekigahara.

333
00:23:54,933 --> 00:23:56,726
Bring them forward!

334
00:24:01,857 --> 00:24:03,358
I'll avenge my humiliation

335
00:24:04,401 --> 00:24:05,652
at Ueda.

336
00:24:08,530 --> 00:24:11,408
Just watch me, Father.

337
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:17,372
By the authority of the Shogun,
I command you!

338
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:20,333
Charge!

339
00:24:54,034 --> 00:24:54,910
Suden.

340
00:24:55,785 --> 00:24:56,828
What's happening?

341
00:24:56,912 --> 00:24:59,789
There appears to be no sign of a revolt.

342
00:24:59,873 --> 00:25:01,750
Our forces are facing fierce resistance.

343
00:25:03,710 --> 00:25:06,213
Then what was that smoke signal?

344
00:25:09,633 --> 00:25:10,842
Don't tell me…

345
00:25:12,928 --> 00:25:15,055
The enemy's falling one after another…

346
00:25:15,138 --> 00:25:16,097
What of the revolt?

347
00:25:16,973 --> 00:25:18,099
What's happened to it?

348
00:25:18,683 --> 00:25:19,768
The revolt…

349
00:25:20,685 --> 00:25:21,811
What happened to it?

350
00:25:21,895 --> 00:25:22,729
Revolt?

351
00:25:23,355 --> 00:25:24,564
Whatever do you mean?

352
00:25:24,648 --> 00:25:26,900
The enemy sent up a smoke signal!

353
00:25:26,983 --> 00:25:28,026
And their banners fell!

354
00:25:28,109 --> 00:25:29,819
Forgive me for keeping you in the dark.

355
00:25:31,321 --> 00:25:33,114
The fallen banners were a ruse.

356
00:25:33,907 --> 00:25:37,077
And the smoke signal
was a trap to lure the enemy in.

357
00:25:38,078 --> 00:25:40,413
We stopped the revolt
before it could begin.

358
00:25:41,706 --> 00:25:45,335
I suspected the enemy was plotting
to turn our men against us.

359
00:25:45,418 --> 00:25:46,962
So I took precautions.

360
00:25:48,129 --> 00:25:49,089
Precautions?

361
00:25:49,172 --> 00:25:53,468
I planted a trusted retainer
among the men stationed at the outpost.

362
00:25:58,098 --> 00:25:59,766
This is the man who led the plot.

363
00:25:59,849 --> 00:26:01,101
Urano!

364
00:26:01,768 --> 00:26:04,145
Well done, Isa, Seikai.

365
00:26:05,188 --> 00:26:06,189
Yes, my lord!

366
00:26:06,273 --> 00:26:09,693
This is the Toyotomi's war.

367
00:26:10,902 --> 00:26:12,487
Do not…

368
00:26:13,613 --> 00:26:14,614
forget your place.

369
00:26:19,119 --> 00:26:20,912
We're back.

370
00:26:21,955 --> 00:26:24,040
There were Tokugawa soldiers everywhere.

371
00:26:24,124 --> 00:26:26,751
You two… I thought you'd left us.

372
00:26:26,835 --> 00:26:28,586
Of course not.

373
00:26:28,670 --> 00:26:31,715
-We were just a little late getting back.
-I figured as much.

374
00:26:34,801 --> 00:26:37,178
That's it. Isa, Seikai.

375
00:26:38,013 --> 00:26:40,598
Let's let everyone think you've deserted.

376
00:26:43,184 --> 00:26:44,936
Ei! Ei! Oh!

377
00:26:45,520 --> 00:26:47,480
Ei! Ei! Oh!

378
00:26:49,065 --> 00:26:49,899
Thanks to them,

379
00:26:50,442 --> 00:26:52,736
we learned of the Tokugawa's plot
ahead of time.

380
00:26:53,653 --> 00:26:54,654
Urano…

381
00:26:56,406 --> 00:26:57,782
why would you do this?

382
00:27:04,289 --> 00:27:07,167
Even if you win this battle,

383
00:27:08,835 --> 00:27:11,171
the Toyotomi clan has no future!

384
00:28:51,438 --> 00:28:52,647
Impressive…

385
00:28:53,982 --> 00:28:55,066
A man's worth

386
00:28:55,817 --> 00:28:58,445
isn't determined solely
by his bloodline or family name.

387
00:29:00,947 --> 00:29:04,117
I suggest you stop
underestimating my Ten Braves.

388
00:29:07,370 --> 00:29:09,706
Raise the banners!

389
00:29:14,544 --> 00:29:18,506
Look! The Sanada banners are flying!

390
00:29:21,342 --> 00:29:23,136
Follow Sanada!

391
00:29:23,219 --> 00:29:24,888
Drive the enemy back!

392
00:29:30,393 --> 00:29:33,104
The Sanada banners have united the men…

393
00:29:34,647 --> 00:29:36,566
It seems my words have inspired them.

394
00:29:47,952 --> 00:29:49,287
Damn you, Sanada!

395
00:29:50,163 --> 00:29:51,247
How dare you!

396
00:29:52,123 --> 00:29:54,584
Hold this position at all costs!

397
00:30:05,512 --> 00:30:07,013
Our men are driving them back.

398
00:30:10,475 --> 00:30:12,310
The rest is up to you, Saizo.

399
00:30:14,270 --> 00:30:15,939
We're ready to withdraw.

400
00:30:22,028 --> 00:30:22,862
Father!

401
00:30:22,946 --> 00:30:26,199
The enemy was waiting for us.
It seems they knew our plan.

402
00:30:26,282 --> 00:30:28,076
Silence! Silence! Silence!

403
00:30:29,160 --> 00:30:30,870
You let yourself be outwitted!

404
00:30:31,746 --> 00:30:33,456
You fool!

405
00:30:36,626 --> 00:30:37,919
Hey!

406
00:30:38,002 --> 00:30:39,754
The Ogosho is returning.

407
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:40,880
TAISEIJI TEMPLE

408
00:31:14,998 --> 00:31:15,915
Did you hear?

409
00:31:15,999 --> 00:31:18,334
Apparently, some strange creature
is locked in the dungeon.

410
00:31:18,418 --> 00:31:20,044
I'd rather not go anywhere near it.

411
00:31:20,128 --> 00:31:20,962
Nor would I.

412
00:31:39,439 --> 00:31:40,273
Sasuke!

413
00:31:41,149 --> 00:31:42,108
Can you move?

414
00:31:43,067 --> 00:31:44,027
Get a hold of yourself!

415
00:31:54,829 --> 00:31:55,663
Hey.

416
00:31:59,626 --> 00:32:02,295
Here. I brought this for you.

417
00:32:14,557 --> 00:32:15,600
Kill him.

418
00:32:16,392 --> 00:32:17,936
He is the enemy.

419
00:32:23,024 --> 00:32:24,025
Yes.

420
00:32:31,866 --> 00:32:35,161
Since when did a monkey like you
start taking orders?

421
00:32:52,595 --> 00:32:53,429
Hey!

422
00:33:17,745 --> 00:33:18,997
Snap out of it.

423
00:33:20,248 --> 00:33:21,124
Sasuke.

424
00:33:23,126 --> 00:33:24,168
Sasuke!

425
00:33:40,935 --> 00:33:41,978
Sasuke.

426
00:33:42,645 --> 00:33:44,272
Kill him.

427
00:33:45,023 --> 00:33:45,940
Kill him!

428
00:33:49,485 --> 00:33:50,862
Shut the hell up, you old hag!

429
00:33:57,660 --> 00:33:59,620
I'm one of the Sanada Ten Braves.

430
00:34:01,372 --> 00:34:03,166
Sarutobi Sasuke.

431
00:34:05,460 --> 00:34:08,087
And I hate being told what to do!

432
00:34:08,713 --> 00:34:10,339
He broke my spell…

433
00:34:11,174 --> 00:34:12,341
through sheer willpower?

434
00:34:12,925 --> 00:34:13,885
You stupid monkey.

435
00:34:14,677 --> 00:34:16,471
You've finally come to your senses?

436
00:34:16,554 --> 00:34:19,807
Why'd you come for me?
I walked out on you.

437
00:34:20,892 --> 00:34:22,435
You really think Lord Yukimura

438
00:34:23,311 --> 00:34:24,395
would abandon you?

439
00:34:26,814 --> 00:34:28,107
Kill them!

440
00:34:31,277 --> 00:34:32,445
Damn it…

441
00:34:33,738 --> 00:34:34,614
Let's go.

442
00:34:38,743 --> 00:34:40,119
What the hell is that?

443
00:34:40,703 --> 00:34:42,246
That's one ugly bird.

444
00:34:55,301 --> 00:34:56,803
-Ieyasu!
-Wait!

445
00:35:45,810 --> 00:35:47,895
I should've killed you after all.

446
00:35:50,189 --> 00:35:51,149
Hey, Saizo.

447
00:35:51,858 --> 00:35:52,984
Let's do that move.

448
00:35:54,485 --> 00:35:55,820
The Saizo Special?

449
00:35:56,654 --> 00:35:58,531
It's the Sasuke Special!

450
00:36:09,292 --> 00:36:10,168
Switch!

451
00:36:10,251 --> 00:36:11,502
SWITCH

452
00:36:16,215 --> 00:36:17,258
Saizo!

453
00:36:33,733 --> 00:36:35,610
You bastard!

454
00:36:39,071 --> 00:36:40,198
Sasuke…

455
00:36:44,160 --> 00:36:45,578
You're strong.

456
00:36:47,663 --> 00:36:48,998
Far stronger than I am.

457
00:36:50,625 --> 00:36:51,500
And you…

458
00:36:53,836 --> 00:36:55,171
You have a place to go home to!

459
00:37:05,389 --> 00:37:07,183
Take care of Lord Yukimura…

460
00:37:08,976 --> 00:37:10,144
You stupid monkey.

461
00:38:15,209 --> 00:38:16,335
Seikai, get down!

462
00:38:21,257 --> 00:38:23,217
Seikai, don't push yourself too hard.

463
00:38:23,968 --> 00:38:24,802
Yeah.

464
00:38:27,847 --> 00:38:29,557
The enemy is retreating!

465
00:38:31,058 --> 00:38:33,060
The first battle is ours.

466
00:38:33,853 --> 00:38:34,687
Indeed.

467
00:38:39,859 --> 00:38:42,194
-You've all fought valiantly!
-Yes, sir!

468
00:38:42,278 --> 00:38:44,697
-Victory belongs to the Toyotomi!
-Yes, sir!

469
00:38:51,078 --> 00:38:53,539
AS OUR FORCES HAVE ALSO SUFFERED LOSSES,

470
00:38:53,622 --> 00:38:55,875
I BELIEVE WE SHOULD SEEK PEACE.

471
00:38:58,586 --> 00:38:59,587
Peace?

472
00:39:04,216 --> 00:39:05,384
Father,

473
00:39:05,468 --> 00:39:08,721
we may have withdrawn,
but we haven't lost.

474
00:39:08,804 --> 00:39:10,598
Isn't it too soon to seek peace?

475
00:39:10,681 --> 00:39:12,433
If we keep fighting, sooner or later…

476
00:39:13,309 --> 00:39:14,852
Sooner or later, we'll win.

477
00:39:15,978 --> 00:39:17,521
And that is precisely the problem.

478
00:39:18,981 --> 00:39:22,276
If word spreads that
even Hideyori can give me trouble,

479
00:39:22,985 --> 00:39:24,862
my reputation will suffer.

480
00:39:24,945 --> 00:39:27,782
-But if the Toyotomi bloodline survives--
-Hidetada.

481
00:39:30,826 --> 00:39:32,828
Who said anything about letting them live?

482
00:39:34,830 --> 00:39:35,790
Ogosho!

483
00:39:37,875 --> 00:39:38,876
It's…

484
00:39:40,753 --> 00:39:42,088
finally awakened!

485
00:39:44,423 --> 00:39:45,466
Is that true?

486
00:39:49,678 --> 00:39:51,013
Wonderful news!

487
00:39:53,766 --> 00:39:56,268
You've all done splendidly.

488
00:39:56,352 --> 00:39:59,605
That's three victories
over the Tokugawa, my lord!

489
00:39:59,688 --> 00:40:01,357
Yes!

490
00:40:01,440 --> 00:40:02,817
It's all thanks to you two.

491
00:40:03,567 --> 00:40:05,361
Well done infiltrating their ranks.

492
00:40:06,487 --> 00:40:08,114
A fine job, Miyoshi brothers.

493
00:40:09,407 --> 00:40:10,366
Glad it all worked out.

494
00:40:10,449 --> 00:40:11,325
Yeah.

495
00:40:11,409 --> 00:40:12,993
That armor looks good on you.

496
00:40:13,077 --> 00:40:14,328
Pardon the interruption.

497
00:40:15,246 --> 00:40:19,208
Lord Ono, Lord Sanada.
Lady Yodo requests your presence.

498
00:40:24,713 --> 00:40:26,298
Think we're getting a reward?

499
00:40:27,133 --> 00:40:28,384
Now that would be nice.

500
00:40:31,512 --> 00:40:32,721
Peace?

501
00:40:32,805 --> 00:40:35,266
The offer came from the Tokugawa side.

502
00:40:35,975 --> 00:40:38,102
All thanks to your valiant efforts.

503
00:40:39,812 --> 00:40:41,730
We mustn't trust Ieyasu.

504
00:40:41,814 --> 00:40:43,315
He must have something up his sleeve.

505
00:40:44,066 --> 00:40:45,317
It could be a trap.

506
00:40:46,610 --> 00:40:50,281
Our victory has shown him
what we're capable of.

507
00:40:50,990 --> 00:40:52,533
You're worrying too much.

508
00:40:54,743 --> 00:40:56,704
Peace is exactly what we want.

509
00:40:57,413 --> 00:40:58,789
This will put an end to the war.

510
00:40:59,290 --> 00:41:00,458
What more could we ask?

511
00:41:01,083 --> 00:41:03,502
I've had quite enough of war.

512
00:41:05,212 --> 00:41:06,922
Surely you agree, Yukimura?

513
00:41:08,257 --> 00:41:10,676
Then allow me to send my ninja

514
00:41:11,427 --> 00:41:13,304
to uncover Ieyasu's true intentions.

515
00:41:13,387 --> 00:41:14,972
Ninja, huh?

516
00:41:15,598 --> 00:41:16,849
They cannot be trusted.

517
00:41:17,975 --> 00:41:19,894
Wouldn't you agree, Lord Ono?

518
00:41:21,687 --> 00:41:22,855
I believe…

519
00:41:25,316 --> 00:41:27,735
we should leave this matter to Sanada.

520
00:41:28,986 --> 00:41:29,820
What?

521
00:41:29,904 --> 00:41:30,738
Harunaga?

522
00:41:31,864 --> 00:41:35,409
We owe our victory to that outpost…

523
00:41:36,202 --> 00:41:38,913
No, to Sanadamaru

524
00:41:39,538 --> 00:41:42,124
and the efforts of Sanada's ninja.

525
00:41:43,083 --> 00:41:44,001
Lord Ono…

526
00:41:46,545 --> 00:41:47,630
We should put our faith…

527
00:41:49,298 --> 00:41:50,257
in them.

528
00:41:54,011 --> 00:41:55,054
Very well.

529
00:41:56,764 --> 00:41:58,349
If Harunaga says so,

530
00:42:00,142 --> 00:42:02,436
we shall determine
the Tokugawa's intentions

531
00:42:03,062 --> 00:42:04,355
before agreeing to peace.

532
00:42:04,438 --> 00:42:06,649
But surely, Lady Yodo…

533
00:42:15,741 --> 00:42:16,742
Sasuke!

534
00:42:17,451 --> 00:42:19,912
You're alive! Thank goodness!

535
00:42:19,995 --> 00:42:24,250
Where the hell have you been?
You had us worried!

536
00:42:24,333 --> 00:42:25,876
The Tokugawa captured me.

537
00:42:25,960 --> 00:42:27,670
How'd you manage to escape?

538
00:42:28,379 --> 00:42:30,256
Saizo came to my rescue.

539
00:42:30,339 --> 00:42:34,051
I knew the bonds of the Sanada
could never be broken.

540
00:42:34,134 --> 00:42:35,386
But…

541
00:42:35,469 --> 00:42:36,387
Where's Saizo?

542
00:42:45,271 --> 00:42:46,355
Sasuke.

543
00:42:50,359 --> 00:42:51,443
Where is Saizo?

544
00:42:56,156 --> 00:42:57,283
Where is he?

545
00:43:06,584 --> 00:43:07,459
I'm sorry.

546
00:43:12,715 --> 00:43:14,174
Saizo's dead.

547
00:43:22,516 --> 00:43:23,642
It's my fault…

548
00:43:26,937 --> 00:43:28,606
He gave his life to save mine…

549
00:44:08,354 --> 00:44:11,523
-What's happening?
-I don't know!

550
00:44:11,607 --> 00:44:12,733
It just came out of nowhere!

551
00:44:15,361 --> 00:44:16,403
Everyone!

552
00:44:17,112 --> 00:44:19,448
Lady Yodo! Please, get back!

553
00:44:19,531 --> 00:44:21,742
-Stay away!
-Please, stand back!

554
00:44:21,825 --> 00:44:23,285
Hey, you saw that, right?

555
00:44:23,369 --> 00:44:25,829
Something flying overhead dropped a bomb.

556
00:44:26,330 --> 00:44:27,956
What the hell was that thing?

557
00:44:28,040 --> 00:44:31,126
Wait, isn't that Lady Yodo's bedchamber?

558
00:44:31,710 --> 00:44:32,878
You don't think…

559
00:44:32,961 --> 00:44:34,797
She was the target?

560
00:44:36,507 --> 00:44:37,591
Write.

561
00:44:37,675 --> 00:44:39,677
Write down everything you've seen.

562
00:44:44,348 --> 00:44:45,724
Enough!

563
00:44:48,143 --> 00:44:49,728
The war is over!

564
00:44:51,438 --> 00:44:52,523
We shall make peace.

565
00:44:53,107 --> 00:44:55,192
Make peace at once!

566
00:45:00,864 --> 00:45:02,116
A fine fit indeed.

567
00:45:02,199 --> 00:45:04,368
Or perhaps this one? What about this?

568
00:45:05,035 --> 00:45:07,663
This is rather splendid too.
How am I to choose?

569
00:45:07,746 --> 00:45:11,917
Surely no ninja alive
could leap higher than this one.

570
00:45:12,709 --> 00:45:13,794
Magnificent.

571
00:45:14,420 --> 00:45:16,505
Truly magnificent, Suden.

572
00:45:17,673 --> 00:45:18,841
You honor me, my lord.

573
00:45:19,925 --> 00:45:22,469
At last, the ninja
we've sought for so long.

574
00:45:23,053 --> 00:45:24,388
One who transcends human limits…

575
00:45:24,888 --> 00:45:26,974
Unrivaled under heaven.

576
00:45:28,517 --> 00:45:33,021
And you, on the other hand…
You let Sasuke escape.

577
00:45:34,606 --> 00:45:35,441
You fool.

578
00:45:44,408 --> 00:45:46,243
-Is anybody there?
-Lord Yukimura!

579
00:45:50,456 --> 00:45:51,290
Someone…

580
00:46:26,074 --> 00:46:31,079
Subtitle translation by: Sayo Takada

581
00:46:31,163 --> 00:46:33,081
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
